node_modules/
# pnpm relocates its content-addressable store next to node_modules when the
# default store dir is on a different filesystem - which is exactly the case in
# the dev container (bind-mounted workspace vs container home, task 046).
.pnpm-store/
dist/
.turbo/
coverage/
.claude/worktrees/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.compose.example
*.log
.DS_Store
# Generated by the isolated full-stack browser-test workflow. This file holds the
# random local-only administrator credential printed by `pnpm docker:up`. It must
# stay ignored under whatever name the harness writes: it was committed once,
# with live values, the moment a rename outran this line.
.e2e-full-stack-credentials.json
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Next 16 writes `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` into each app directory at build time
# (`next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js`). They are generated, not authored,
# and their text carries em dashes that `check:no-em-dash` correctly refuses, so a
# `git add -A` after a browser run reds the gate with a file nobody wrote. Ignored
# rather than fought: deleting them only re-creates them on the next run.
#
# THIS IS A STOPGAP, NOT THE CHOSEN FIX. It is the subject of open issue #431, which
# awaits a Code Owner decision between (a) ignoring the generator's output, which is
# what this rule does, and (b) suppressing the generation itself. (b) is the more
# durable of the two, because ignoring leaves em-dash-bearing files on disk in a repo
# whose gate exists to keep them out: this rule hides them from `git status`, it does
# not remove them. #431 can replace it without touching anything else here.
#
# Landed on its own because the trap cost four separate sessions in one day, and the
# generated file's own text argues the reader into committing it.
apps/*/AGENTS.md
apps/*/CLAUDE.md
